ublk: implement buffer pool registration (UBLK_U_IO_ADD_BUF_POOL)

Implement the uring_cmd handler for UBLK_U_IO_ADD_BUF_POOL which
allows the server to register buffer pools per queue before the first
FETCH_REQ.

The config is passed via a userspace pointer in ublksrv_io_cmd.addr.
Each pool is validated (page-aligned addr/buf_size, no duplicate sizes,
< UBLK_MAX_BUF_POOLS per queue) and inserted sorted by buf_size into
the queue's buf_pools array.

When UBLK_F_PINNED_BUFS is set, the buffer region is pinned via
pin_user_pages_fast(FOLL_WRITE | FOLL_LONGTERM), accounted against
RLIMIT_MEMLOCK (bypassable with CAP_IPC_LOCK), and vmapped for kernel
access. This follows the same pattern as fuse's fuse_bufring_pin_mem().

